  ('a478cb82-323d-5bea-b245-d40e80d0b495', 'nuance-debate', 'He said the report was <b>competent</b>, which felt like damning it with faint praise.', 'C1', 0),
  ('015711c5-e091-5aba-b008-5087f8e3d377', 'nuance-debate', 'Calling her performance “adequate” is <b>damning her with faint praise</b>.', 'C1', 1),
  ('120ebc4b-8822-5e93-b1cf-6e588751f8e7', 'nuance-debate', 'I don''t want to <b>damn the whole thing with faint praise</b>, but it was fine at best.', 'C2', 2),
  ('832a055f-4c8c-5d25-a41d-03217bd029d8', 'nuance-debate', 'Once the funding fell through, the outcome was <b>a foregone conclusion</b>.', 'C1', 3),
  ('9b247f8c-84c2-5902-8990-6f3f1b580790', 'nuance-debate', 'Everyone treated his promotion as <b>a foregone conclusion</b>, which annoyed the other candidates.', 'C2', 4),
  ('f8c692d9-4d62-532d-acd6-7e27f9a00ffc', 'nuance-debate', 'Nothing here is <b>a foregone conclusion</b> until the board actually votes.', 'B2', 5),
  ('abb919ae-df89-5050-a0e1-cbec2902f0a8', 'nuance-debate', 'We''re <b>splitting hairs</b> over wording when the whole section needs rewriting.', 'C1', 6),
  ('ddb6bd03-6aff-5ef7-8a5b-813ff42ee75e', 'nuance-debate', 'I don''t want to <b>split hairs</b>, but there''s a real difference between the two.', 'C1', 7),
  ('7f97fb6f-f6cc-5f82-8258-6d83b1e207e6', 'nuance-debate', 'That distinction isn''t <b>splitting hairs</b> — it changes who is liable.', 'C1', 8),
  ('48addb92-1368-5b41-b00c-953523382cf4', 'nuance-debate', 'They''re <b>hedging their bets</b> by running both suppliers for another quarter.', 'C1', 9),
  ('6b94350a-20a9-587f-814f-9c1bba1bca4c', 'nuance-debate', 'Stop <b>hedging your bets</b> and tell me which one you''d actually choose.', 'C1', 10),
  ('fe0b3895-3172-5698-8b18-76d4d8369098', 'nuance-debate', 'His answer <b>hedged</b> so carefully that I still don''t know his position.', 'C1', 11),
  ('a969c216-9054-5782-aa1c-b467888dc333', 'nuance-debate', 'Saying it must be true because nobody disproved it rather <b>begs the question</b>.', 'C1', 12),
  ('0c015f3e-0fc7-5fe8-8924-342fbc3133e0', 'nuance-debate', 'That argument <b>begs the question</b>: it assumes exactly what it sets out to show.', 'B2', 13),
  ('e5e12dfe-8b2b-5bd1-af72-fe693eab322e', 'nuance-debate', 'Careful — you''re using “<b>begs the question</b>” to mean “raises the question”.', 'C1', 14),
  ('0fab176c-4342-571e-b039-3ba602cc7eba', 'nuance-debate', 'Remote work is <b>a double-edged sword</b>: more focus, far less serendipity.', 'C1', 15),
  ('8b073b52-5f26-5539-b32d-aea0d26fa29b', 'nuance-debate', 'Her bluntness is <b>a double-edged sword</b> in negotiations.', 'C1', 16),
  ('3d20af3e-9979-59c8-98f2-673c6b9e59bb', 'nuance-debate', 'Any rule that rigid is <b>a double-edged sword</b>, and we''ll feel the other edge eventually.', 'C2', 17),
  ('96fe40b7-9fdc-5ebe-9772-d899985ca5f4', 'nuance-debate', 'Another reorganisation just <b>papers over the cracks</b> in how we hire.', 'B2', 18),
  ('2c5439a0-5bd2-5e80-98d6-9b4e358f94e9', 'nuance-debate', 'We keep <b>papering over the cracks</b> instead of fixing the architecture.', 'B2', 19),
  ('f746c307-6873-5eb2-a7b0-0cbee00b25c9', 'nuance-debate', 'That apology <b>papered over the cracks</b> without addressing what caused them.', 'B2', 20),
  ('2c938a04-49dd-57dc-ad30-7ed696b9e23b', 'nuance-debate', 'Nobody wants to name <b>the elephant in the room</b>, which is that the launch date is fiction.', 'B2', 21),
  ('aae2c172-fe66-552e-b25f-8bdb5babff00', 'nuance-debate', 'Let''s address <b>the elephant in the room</b> before we go through the slides.', 'B2', 22),
  ('9de60fcb-865e-541f-bf28-fcfa9ddbc6ec', 'nuance-debate', 'His absence was <b>the elephant in the room</b> for the entire meeting.', 'B1', 23),
  ('d6516229-3593-5096-b754-7ddd8520c086', 'nuance-debate', 'Explaining the benefits of testing here is <b>preaching to the choir</b>.', 'B2', 24),
  ('a64274a2-7013-52b8-bf93-d952390ac56f', 'nuance-debate', 'I know I''m <b>preaching to the choir</b>, but the point bears repeating outside this room.', 'C2', 25),
  ('7b80f056-adc5-568d-af7a-b609bb24dc07', 'nuance-debate', 'That whole campaign ended up <b>preaching to the choir</b> and persuading nobody new.', 'C1', 26),
  ('626e4feb-5d9d-5940-8aa6-ace9d012d130', 'nuance-debate', 'They won the case, but the legal fees made it <b>a pyrrhic victory</b>.', 'B2', 27),
  ('f58cb607-df84-5792-b9e5-e80b18afd93f', 'nuance-debate', 'Cutting the team to hit the date would be <b>a pyrrhic victory</b>.', 'B2', 28),
  ('86a0440c-9291-5d0f-8a1c-f6a3bad45034', 'nuance-debate', 'It felt like <b>a pyrrhic victory</b> — we were right, and it cost us the client.', 'B2', 29)
